div.p:
A typical example was Pravda of June 30 which
                    arrayed together, in two adjoining columns, Tass reports under the following
                    headlines: “Anglo-American Economic Contradictions”; “Harriman Confers with Cripps”;
                    “Reduction of Britain’s Dollar and Gold Reserves”; “Plow They Maintain High
                    Prices in Denmark”; “Deterioration of Economic Situation in United States”;
                    “Share Prices Fall on New York Market”; “Deficit in Budget of U.S. Government”;
                    and “Catastrophic Financial Situation in South Baden”.
